<header class="page-header">
  <h1>About SLP WOW</h1>
</header>

<p><strong>SLP WOW</strong> (slpwow.com) is a professional community site for speech-language pathologists in the United States and allied settings. We publish news you can use between sessions, index free resources with honest implementation notes, and maintain word-list structures you can extend in your own materials.</p>

<h2>Who this is for</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Licensed SLPs in schools, hospitals, outpatient clinics, early intervention, and telepractice</li>
  <li>Clinical fellows and graduate clinicians under supervision</li>
  <li>Related professionals collaborating on communication goals — when content is clearly labeled</li>
</ul>

<h2>Who this is not for</h2>
<p>We do not target caregivers or clients as the primary audience. Family education belongs in your local context, your employer’s templates, and your clinical judgement — not generic blog posts pretending to be treatment.</p>

<h2>Editorial standards</h2>
<p>Research roundups cite primary or peer-reviewed sources where possible. Clinical tips describe general strategies, not individualized recommendations. Resource posts disclose limitations, licensing, and documentation considerations.</p>

<h2>Independence</h2>
<p>SLP WOW community content is separate from unrelated infrastructure projects in this repository. See <code>sites/slpwow/SCOPE.md</code> for the legal and scope boundary.</p>

